"""Approximate the component as a sentence-opening cue.

After a period, capitalized words (and uncased letters) get a pulse, strongest
for familiar clause openers and smaller for common transition words. Ordinary
articles and pronouns get a modest pulse; lowercase continuations get a slight
negative value. Other sentence-ending marks produce a weaker opener pulse.
