"""A lexical degree/quantity signal, dominated by the word 'more'.

It gives weaker signed responses to related quantity and alternative words,
how/what, 'after', and several translations. Capitalization and leading
whitespace change the strength. Familiar phrases ('no more', 'once more', 'or more', 'each other')
reduce it. Unlisted spellings get zero, leaving small background responses
unmodeled. Previous-token context resets at every document boundary.
"""
