"""Component layers.0.mlp.down_proj:867: a "back" detector.

Almost always silent. It fires on the English word "back" (" back", "Back",
"backs", "backed", "backing", "BACK") at a strong, fairly constant level
(about 2.3), and on the Chinese character 背 (back, as in the body part or to
carry) more strongly still. Weaker responses come from words of the same
sense: "backward(s)", "backup" and other back- compounds (about 1), and
"background", "behind", "rear" words for the back of the body, such as belly
and buttock words, plus "back" in other languages ("zurück", "назад", "lưng")
(about 0.5 to 1). Everything else gets 0.

The value depends only on the newest token, so the program keeps no state.
