Single 视/視 characters respond more strongly than whole sight-related words.
Video/visual word families and audiovisual vocabulary give smaller responses;
case, spacing, and inflection change their strength. A few attention words and
chat markers have minor responses. This detects token forms, not passage topics,
and deliberately omits many weak, idiosyncratic lexical effects.
"""
READS = ()

AUDIOVISUAL_HAN = {
    '电视', '電視', '影视', '影視', '视觉', '視覺', '视听', '視聽',
